The attached image, Figure 9 from Journal of Controlled Release 204 (2015) 51-59 (and Figure 1 from npj Vaccines (2017)2:4), illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the antibody response to adsorbed antigen. The box plots show anti-rPA IgG titers in mice immunized with rPA alone or combined with aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11 at different doses (200, 50, 12.5 µg). Nano-11 formulations, particularly at lower doses, induce antibody titers comparable to or greater than AH, with the 12.5 µg Nano-11 dose showing a significantly stronger response than the corresponding AH dose. This demonstrates Nano-11's effectiveness as a vaccine adjuvant in enhancing humoral immunity.